## SEVERITY / VERDICT
Blocker: any path beyond the one, or any byte under `api/src`/`.github`/`infra`; a skip/removal/weakened assertion; T1 or T2 leaves the 500 test or the twin GREEN (the commission's Done-when is not met); either pin red unmutated at head, in Debug or in Release; a name lost; a warning or error at head that base does not have; the whole project or an api solution test red at head that is green at base; a secret; a merge conflict; overlap with any live branch > 0; a flaky pin (a red in the 10 repeats). Major: P1 or P2 or P4 leaves a pin green (the pin does not hold what it says); P3 green without a probe showing equivalence; a builder claim your measurement contradicts (32 tests, 303/0/0, 0 warnings, 2 red each, 1 fire per request, a quoted boundary on the wire); T3 (mBn) no longer red 2 (the control broke); the instrument control not firing (base file also red under T1/T2, or head file green at base under no mutant is expected and is not that). Minor: a test title that no longer says what the test asserts (the 500 test's and the twin's titles do not mention the stack pin); the shared-method limit (T5 green) if the builder did not disclose it (it did: Note); an undisclosed extra residual; an unclear failure message. **Notes (NOT failures):** no CI on a PR-less branch; the pins couple to a private method name in `api/src` (rename turns both red, by design); `ReadBoundedAsync` serves both parts (T5); CodeQL not run; the SQL Server shard is CI's. Overall **GO** · **GO WITH FINDINGS** · **NO GO**. First line of STATUS: `GATE VERDICT B464: <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> @ b9fd28e (delta <1 path, 1 commit, api/src+.github+infra 0 bytes y/n, skips 0 y/n> · prior work <history matches y/n, line facts corrected n> · mutants <T1-T4 + P1-P4 killed n of 8, survivors <names|none>, base-file T1/T2 survive y/n, head-file T1/T2 red 2 y/n, T5 <green=disclosed|red>> · suites <Feedback project n/n/n head vs n/n/n base, names lost n added n, warnings n vs n, Release class n/32, 10 repeats n/10, api solution <n/n|NOT RUN>> · merge <clean|conflict>, overlap telemetry n, b459 n, b461 <n|branch absent>, b462 <n|branch absent> · CI <none|state> · gitleaks rc <n>)`. Then Step 0 sha256s and slot count · REFUSE counts · PINS (start, mid, verdict: branch name beside each sha, the other seats' branches read only to show them unmoved by you) · instrument (dotnet version, Release/Debug, load per heavy start, time waited) · checks 1-5 each with FAIL (clock), evidence path, result · findings `B464-n` (severity, `path:line` at the head, instrument, FAIL met, fix-shape in prose, evidence class MEASURED AT RUNTIME / PROBED / READ ONLY) · FOR TUESDAY (no PR yet: Tuesday opens it on GO/GWF and CodeQL runs on it; HPSMPOC-306's text could note that the ticket's first suggested shape, "fired after the whole head", does not separate the mutants; the next `ReadBoundedAsync` rename will turn two tests red) · FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections / processes and trees left · **UNMEASURED**. **Last line, exactly:** `VERDICT: B464 b460/hpsmpoc-306-carrier-boundary-pins @ b9fd28e on main <sha7>: HPSMPOC-306 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO> (no PR yet: CodeQL not run)` (main by `ls-remote` at verdict) or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`.

